  "texts": {
    "preamble": "A.Vasanth vs The District Revenue Officer/ on 8 February, 2019 Author: K.Ravichandrabaabu Bench: K.Ravichandrabaabu",
    "facts": "2. The petitioners are aggrieved against the proceedings of the first respondent dated 05.09.2018 imposing penalty on them under the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 along with Rules and Regulations, 2011.",
    "arguments": ". However, the learned counsel for the petitioners submitted that the said impugned orders were received by the petitioners only on 14.01.2019 and to the petitioners' knowledge, the said Tribunal is not functioning. Therefore, he contended that the present writ petitions can be entertained. 5. On the other hand, the learned Special Government Pleader for the respondents, based on instructions from the Food Safety Officer, Mr.S.Sasikumar, who is personally present before this Court, submitted that the Tribunal started to function from 01.02.2019 onwards and therefore, the petitioners can very well approach the Tribunal and file an appeal.",
    "petitioner_arguments": ". However, the learned counsel for the petitioners submitted that the said impugned orders were received by the petitioners only on 14.01.2019 and to the petitioners' knowledge, the said Tribunal is not functioning. Therefore, he contended that the present writ petitions can be entertained. 5. On the other hand, the learned Special Government Pleader for the respondents, based on instructions from the Food Safety Officer, Mr.S.Sasikumar, who is personally present before this Court, submitted that the Tribunal started to function from 01.02.2019 onwards and therefore, the petitioners can very well approach the Tribunal and file an appeal.",
